# Pinned spec commit

This reference implementation implements the PayTP formal interop specification
(`spec/formal/`, rules F1–F10) at the exact spec commit pinned below. The formal
spec is the source of truth: where the code and the spec disagree, the spec wins.

    repo:   paytp-spec
    commit: a4e6887
    branch: main
    date:   2026-07-16

Conformance delta since the prior pin (`8dfa786`): the only `spec/formal/` change is the
whitepaper version marker (v0.29 → **v0.30**, the published review draft) — no F1–F10 rule
changed, so the conformance corpus is unaffected. The RI implements the spec's secure Tier-0
model: F2-k origin authentication (`AcceptedBinding` / `accept_origin`), **both** F4-e modes —
the compat single-leg baseline (settlement-authoritative Design A, `Wallet::pay_baseline`) and
the secure two-leg (`Wallet::plan_two_leg`) — the F3-a mirror rule enforced on the wallet pay
path (`Wallet::pay_baseline` requires a signed offer that mirrors the approved outer `accepts[]`
entry), and the F9.3 REVOKED LEB128 annotation. The F4-e compat single-leg's payer-vs-payer
redirect residual is a **stated, bounded** property of that mode (protocol-accounting-safe, not
business-safe), not an exclusion. Scope limits stay as declared in `SCOPE.md`.

The formal spec and the whitepaper are published at:

  - Formal spec (the `Fx.y` / `Fx-y` anchors referenced throughout this code):
    https://paytp.org/spec
  - Whitepaper (the `§x.y` anchors):
    https://paytp.org/whitepaper

Anchor legend for comments in this repository:

  - `Fx.y` / `Fx-y` — a rule in the formal spec (paytp.org/spec).
  - `§x.y`         — a section of the whitepaper (paytp.org/whitepaper).

The conformance-vector corpus in `conformance/` and the rule→test index in
`conformance/COVERAGE.md` map each shipped spec rule to the executable test that
exercises it, all against the pinned commit above.
